Changes code from Helium's helium/core/add-native-bangs.patch (GPL-3.0, The Helium Authors).

Helium's !bangs come from its services (<services base>/bangs.json, behind consent). Solara never turns the services
on, and its address bar is its own (packages/core), so Chromium's omnibox never uses bangs. Helium 0.20.3 already
skips the fetch while the services are off; LoadBangs now answers at once with no bangs whatever the prefs say, so no
loader is made, nothing is requested and no retry is scheduled. The rest of the bangs code stays and compiles.

--- a/components/search_engines/template_url_bang_manager.cc
+++ b/components/search_engines/template_url_bang_manager.cc
@@ -184,13 +184,7 @@
   weak_ptr_factory_.InvalidateWeakPtrs();
   backoff_.Reset();
   callback_ = std::move(callback);
-
-  if (!helium::ShouldFetchBangs(*prefs_)) {
-    OnBangsLoaded(base::MakeRefCounted<Catalogue>(std::vector<Bang>()));
-    return;
-  }
-
-  StartFetch();
+  OnBangsLoaded(base::MakeRefCounted<Catalogue>(std::vector<Bang>()));
 }
 
 void BangManager::StartFetch() {
